---
title: List projection guards
description: CI guards for bounded repository list reads and OpenAPI list response contracts (Audit Point 15).
---

# List projection guards

Codifies performance standards for **operator bookings** and **tour** list paths: repository `findMany` must be bounded or projected, and public list OpenAPI schemas must not expose internal JSON blobs.

## Repository guard — `guard:unbounded-list`

**Script:** [`scripts/guards/guard-unbounded-list.mjs`](../../scripts/guards/guard-unbounded-list.mjs)

**Scope:** `apps/api/src/**/*.repository.ts` (excludes `platform/` admin repos and `in-memory-*.repository.ts`)

**Rule:** Every tenant-scoped `*.findMany` call (see delegate list in guard script) must include **`take:`**. `select:` alone (full tenant scan) **FAILs**. Bounded `where.in` with a documented caller cap is also accepted.

**Legacy allowlist:** Empty — finance, exposure profile seeding, and workspace draft snapshots were remediated in the performance backlog (2026-07-07). New deferrals require an explicit doc entry and guard allowlist line.

**Delegates scanned:** `operatorRegistration`, `tour`, `userTenant`, `operatorPendingInvite`, `operatorSettingsAuditEvent`, `integrationConnection`, `integrationEventPolicy`, `workspaceDraftEvent`, `outboxEvent`, and other tenant models — see [`guard-unbounded-list.mjs`](../../scripts/guards/guard-unbounded-list.mjs).

## Bookings duplicate-finder paths (AP15 — Faz 2)

Guest duplicate checks run in `BookingsService` over bounded `listByTenant` (status ≠ cancelled|rejected). Dedicated `findActiveDuplicateBy*` repository methods were **removed** (no production callers on the Booking port).

User directory summary (`getWorkspaceUserBookingSummary`) uses **SQL counts** plus `listRecentBySubmittedUser(tenantId, userId, MAX_MEMBER_BOOKINGS_RECENT_TRIPS)` — not a full member booking scan.

`listByTenant` is **deprecated** — delegates to `listByTenantPage` with `MAX_BOOKINGS_LIST_BY_TENANT_DEPRECATED` (500), not an unbounded scan. `listRecentBySubmittedUser` is capped at `MAX_MEMBER_BOOKINGS_LIST_CAP` (500).

Constants: `bookings-member-summary-projection.ts`.

**Static checks:** `test/bookings-member-summary-projection.spec.ts` (BK-MEM-01..03)

## Finance registration invoice facts (AP15 — P1)

`getRegistrationInvoiceFacts` must not full-scan payments or prepayment outbox rows per registration.

| Path | Bound / aggregate |
|------|-------------------|
| Prepayment sum | SQL `SUM` on `outbox_events.payload->>'amountMinor'` |
| Paid sum | SQL `SUM` on `payments.amount` where `status = 'Paid'` |
| `paymentAmountsMinor` | `findMany` + `take: MAX_PAYMENTS_PER_REGISTRATION` (50) |
| `findPaymentStatusesByRegistration` | same cap |

Shared helper: `finance/load-registration-invoice-facts.ts` · constants: `finance-list-projection.ts`.

**Static checks:** `test/finance-invoice.spec.ts` (integration, requires Postgres) · `test/finance-registration-invoice-facts.spec.ts` (FIN-INV-01..03)

## Identity directory / invites (AP15 — Phase 5)

Tenant-scoped membership and pending-invite lists must not use unbounded `findMany`. Repository constants live in `identity-list-projection.ts`:

| Method | Bound | Projection |
|--------|-------|------------|
| `listMembershipsByTenant` | `take: MAX_IDENTITY_MEMBERSHIPS_PER_TENANT` (500) | `MEMBERSHIP_LIST_SELECT` |
| `listMembershipsWithUsersByTenant` | same | membership select + `user: { select: { id, mobile } }` |
| `listPendingInvitesByTenant` | `take: MAX_PENDING_INVITES_PER_TENANT` (200) | `PENDING_INVITE_LIST_SELECT` |
| `findPendingInviteByPhone` | `findFirst` (no list scan) | `PENDING_INVITE_LIST_SELECT` |

All paths remain under `withTenantRls(tenantId, …)` — RLS policies unchanged.

**Static checks:** `test/identity-list-projection.spec.ts` (ID-LIST-01..03)

## Settings audit trail (AP15 — P1)

Append-only `operatorSettingsAuditEvent` reads must not scan unbounded rows.

| Method | Bound | Projection / pagination |
|--------|-------|-------------------------|
| `listByTenantPage` | `take: limit + 1` (max 500) | `SETTINGS_AUDIT_LIST_SELECT` + keyset `(occurredAt desc, id desc)` |
| `listByTenant` | delegates to page with `MAX_SETTINGS_AUDIT_EVENTS_PER_TENANT` | same select |

Constants: `settings-audit-list-projection.ts`.

**Static checks:** `test/settings-audit-list-projection.spec.ts` (SET-AUD-01..03)

## Integration connection lists (AP15 — P1)

List paths must **not** load `credentials` Json from Postgres. Detail paths (`findFirst` / `findUnique` by id) may load full rows.

| Method | Bound | Projection |
|--------|-------|------------|
| `listForWorkspace` | `take: MAX_INTEGRATION_CONNECTIONS_PER_WORKSPACE` (50) | `INTEGRATION_CONNECTION_LIST_SELECT` |
| `listEnabledConnectionsForScope` | same cap | same select (policy engine uses capabilities, not credentials) |
| `listPoliciesForConnection` | `take: MAX_INTEGRATION_EVENT_POLICIES_PER_CONNECTION` (100) | `INTEGRATION_EVENT_POLICY_LIST_SELECT` |

Constants: `integration-list-projection.ts`.

**Static checks:** `test/integration-list-projection.spec.ts` (INT-LIST-01..03)

## Workspace draft events (AP15 — P1)

`listByDraft` must push `take: limit` and `orderBy` into SQL — no fetch-all + in-memory `.slice()`.

| Method | Bound | Order |
|--------|-------|-------|
| `listByDraft` | `take: limit` (service clamps 1..100) | `occurredAt desc`, `id desc` |

**Static checks:** `test/workspace-draft-events-list.spec.ts` (DRF-EVT-01..02)

## Bookings outbox by aggregate (AP15 — P1)

`listOutboxByAggregate` was **removed** from `BookingRepositoryPort` (no production callers). Mutate paths still enqueue outbox rows under tenant TX. Memory tests may use `peekOutboxByAggregateForTests` (not on the port). Cap constant retained in `bookings-outbox-projection.ts` for that helper / future platform reads.

**Static checks:** `booking-outbox-tenant-boundary.spec.ts`

